      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T18:05:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rather nit: \"stage-2\" is generally not an x86 term... And in the upstream pKVM-ARM code this field is named `pkvm_memcache` instead, thus we probably don\u0027t need to be particularly attached to the name `stage2_mc`. So we can make this name more consistent with our other naming, e.g. something like `guest_mmu_memcache`?",
      "revId": "7771b67e8c9527853bf7a3951b913a9c88846e8a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b9a7c20_1246dd0c",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1112,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T19:06:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So we can make this name more consistent with our other naming, e.g. something like guest_mmu_memcache?\n\nOr maybe just `memcache` (if it will be a sub-field of a structure field `pkvm`), why not. It we have any other use cases for a per-vCPU memcache in the future, I imagine we may reuse this memcache for that, instead of introducing a separate one.",
      "parentUuid": "b8f42c24_13f3fc33",
      "revId": "7771b67e8c9527853bf7a3951b913a9c88846e8a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "438b27ad_b74d31d5",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1112,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-27T08:14:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Similar to https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/3702536/comment/75cd0329_cf0ad8ef/ and https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/3702536/comment/bbae1fc3_7e929419/ - using dedicate memcache for stage2 mmu pages is rather desired due kvm_account_pgtable_pages usage.\n\nRegarding the name, maybe: `guest_tdp_memcache`?",
      "parentUuid": "8b9a7c20_1246dd0c",
      "revId": "7771b67e8c9527853bf7a3951b913a9c88846e8a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21b0b8d2_3e7d2f47",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1112,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-27T13:45:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I see.\n\nRegarding the name, how about just `mmu_memcache` or `mmu_mc`? We don\u0027t necessarily need to make it super-explanatory, so we can keep it short, and also I\u0027ve realized that using \"guest\" in KVM-high MMU context might make it ambiguous with nested VMs MMU - see e.g. `guest_mmu` field in struct kvm_vcpu_arch.\n\nRegarding \"tdp\", we don\u0027t generally use this term in pKVM code (where is it not as relevant as in traditional KVM, since pKVM _requires_ 2 stages, and so on; in 6.15+ we consistently use names hyp_mmu, host_mmu, guest_mmu instead).",
      "parentUuid": "438b27ad_b74d31d5",
      "revId": "7771b67e8c9527853bf7a3951b913a9c88846e8a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24273851_63a74c2f",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1112,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-28T11:47:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, as we also discuss offline and agreed, seems like `guest_mmu_memcache` is the best option and I will go with it.",
      "parentUuid": "21b0b8d2_3e7d2f47",
      "revId": "7771b67e8c9527853bf7a3951b913a9c88846e8a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96b050e4_985f7451",
        "filename": "arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1113,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-17T17:20:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would make sense to put both pkvm_vcpu_handle and stage2_mc into a structure field e.g. `struct kvm_protected_vcpu pkvm` similar to `struct kvm_protected_vm pkvm` in struct kvm_arch?\n\nAlthough while we\u0027re at it, `kvm_protected_vm` seems a misnomer, since it is not just about protected VMs. We could rename it e.g. to `kvm_pkvm_vm` (and if so, also `kvm_pkvm_vcpu` instead of `kvm_protected_vcpu`).",
      "revId": "7771b67e8c9527853bf7a3951b913a9c88846e8a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
